Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 04:26:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] feat: measured mandate checkout (limits, prepare + hold
 nonce, evidenced receipt)

brain.md S2 / B3, server part: a bounded, evidenced checkout that only the 1 s hold can pay.

- mandate.py: IntentMandate (one per session in data/mandates/intents/, 24 h: budget cap on the
  order total, delivery deadline, seller policy, the instruction text and a change history;
  voice can only tighten, the panel may loosen or clear), CartMandate (part line units -> packs,
  BOM lines, shipping, total, the headset's evidence; hash = sha256 of canonical JSON; saved in
  data/mandates/carts/), the checks (price re-read, within limit, delivery by the deadline,
  quantity evidence, structured seller listing, fit, card) as ok / warn / fail, and in-memory
  hold nonces (single-use, 120 s, bound to cart hash + session, a newer prepare revokes).
- POST /commerce/limits: only the fields sent change; a looser voice ask comes back in `refused`.
- POST /checkout/prepare: prices the cart on the server, returns the cart, cart_hash, checks,
  all_ok and the hold nonce. Never pays.
- POST /checkout: with cart_hash + hold_nonce + hold_ms (>= 1000) + session_id it redeems the
  nonce, requires the request to match the prepared cart and the price to be unchanged (rebuilt
  hash), re-runs the checks against the current limits, and adds receipt.mandate {intent, cart,
  authorization (with hold_ms), evidence, checks}. 400 missing/short proof, 409 stale/reused/
  foreign/tampered, 422 a check fails. The sandbox request carries the cart hash as
  clientReferenceInformation.code and intent id / evidence / session as merchantDefinedInformation.
  Offline receipts (no Cybersource keys) keep their honest label and carry the same chain.
- REQUIRE_HOLD_PROOF (default false): true refuses a /checkout without the proof. Off by default
  so the current app build can still check out until it sends the proof.
- api.md: both endpoints, the proof fields, errors and the receipt's mandate block.

Not in this patch (S2's cut order): TAP request signing / JWKS and the phase-2 payment link.

Rebased onto integration/grok-all (c706f13): `checkout.authorize` takes both F6's
`safety_verdict` and our `mandate`; the receipt keeps F6's verdict and F5's `postcard_url` and
adds `mandate`; `/checkout` keeps the `bom_id` notebook entry and F9's manual prefetch, and
records the cart's receipt after a proof-verified payment. The flow diagram keeps F5's postcard
call before prepare. Test: the proof receipt keeps the Grok fields.

